DEF("case:prohibited-qualified-by-a-unary", S2(A("cmd:deo_viols"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("state:deontics"), S1(S1(S3(A("DEO:p:MessageRecommendsAPI#1"), A("prohibited"), S2(A("MessageRecommendsAPI"), S5(A("joinon"), A("MessageRecommendsAPI"), A("APIIsInternal"), S1(S2(N(2), N(1))), S2(N(1), N(2)))))))), S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("MessageRecommendsAPI"), S2(S2(A("m1"), A("/ymm/")), S2(A("m2"), A("/vin/")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("APIIsInternal"), S1(S1(A("/ymm/"))))))))),
"THE SCREEN'S ACTIONS ARE THE MACHINE TABLE THE API READS (2026-09-09). The screen built its own transition table from the addressed machine alone, so a ticket at A, a working state of the nested Open machine, was offered nothing: advance is defined in Open and close is inherited from it. The actions section now reads main:machine_trs, scoped to the noun's machines and carrying the inherited rows, so the screen at A offers advance and close, as the API does.",
"A DEONTIC SCOPED ON A SUPERTYPE BINDS EVERY SUBTYPE INSTANCE (2026-09-18). Response carries the rule and Support Response carries the instance, which is support.auto.dev exactly: a supertype introduced to hold thirty-two drafting rules has no roles of its own, so no create ever files an id under it and the rule bound nothing and said nothing. The first two are the same population read twice, as the deontic reads it and as ui:ids answers it; at HEAD both are empty. The third is the guard against reading the cone upward: the rule on the SUBTYPE and the instance filed under the SUPERTYPE must stay quiet, because an id known only to be a Response is not known to be a Support Response, and it answers the empty list before and after.",
DEF("fixture:supertype-deontic",
    K(S6(S3(A("CELL"), A("state:fts"), S1(S1(S5(A("ResponseIsNatural"), S1(A("Response")), S1(S1(N(1))), PHI(), S1(PHI()))))), S3(A("CELL"), A("state:declared"), S1(S1(S2(A("ResponseIsNatural"), S1(A("Response")))))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S1(S2(A("r1"), A("Support Response")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("state:deontics"), S1(S1(S3(A("DEO:m:ResponseIsNatural#1"), A("mandatory"), S1(S2(A("ResponseIsNatural"), N(1))))))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeIsSubtypeOfObjectType"), S1(S2(A("Support Response"), A("Response")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S1(S3(A("CELL"), A("ResponseIsNatural"), PHI())))))),
