    S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("cmd:deo_viols"), A("fixture:subtype-deontic")), PHI())),

"AND A CREATE OF A SUBTYPE INSTANCE ANSWERS THE SUPERTYPE-S OBLIGATION, 200 AND NOT 201 (2026-09-18). These two fixtures differ in ONE ROW -- whether Widget is a subtype of Thing -- and nothing else: the same create of the same Widget answers committed without the row and committed_with_violations with it, because each Thing is obliged to belong to a Domain and a Widget is a Thing. http:status maps the first to 201 and the second to 200, both of them commits, and main:create_outcome refuses only on an alethic one. That move is what the cone did to the base store the moment the population stopped being a name lookup: Stream is a subtype of Function, Function belongs to Domain is a deontic mandatory on the FFP root whose cone is 112 of the 131 object types, and a created Stream that belongs to no Domain is the 321st standing violation of a rule that already had 320. The rule is not new and neither is the entity-s type; only the arithmetic that had been skipping it is. Pinned here rather than in a host test so that a status assertion elsewhere is known to be about boot writeback and not about this.",
