    K(S3(S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S1(S2(A("sr1"), A("Support Request")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("StateMachineDefinitionIsForObjectType"), S2(S2(A("Request"), A("Request")), S2(A("Support Request"), A("Support Request")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeIsSubtypeOfObjectType"), S1(S2(A("Support Request"), A("Request"))))))),
DEF("case:entity-machine-prefers-the-more-specific-type", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("ui:machine_type"), S4(A("CONS"), A("fixture:machine-cone"), K(A("Request")), K(A("sr1")))), PHI())),
"THE VERB ANSWERS THE AFFORDANCES OF THE ENTITY IT NAMES (2026-09-17). actions was system:view_menu itself and the model declared it to accept the store, so the route dropped the id and every entity of every store answered the empty menu. These three pin the verb over the pair it takes now: a started ticket standing at A, a working state of the nested Open machine, is offered advance and the inherited close; a Support Request whose machine is declared for the SUBTYPE, and whose id sits in the Request population too, is offered its own machine's accept and the outer machine's inherited resolve, which is the shape that made a real support queue offer nothing; and an id no machine holds is offered an empty menu rather than failing. The first two answered the empty menu before this, the third answered it for the right reason.",
DEF("fixture:subtype-machine",
    K(S(S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition"), S1(S2(A("Open"), A("Open")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S2(S2(A("sr1"), A("Request")), S2(A("sr1"), A("Support Request")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("StateMachineDefinitionIsForObjectType"), S1(S2(A("Support Request"), A("Support Request")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusIsInitialInStateMachineDefinition"), S2(S2(A("Open"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("Received"), A("Open")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition"), S4(S2(A("Open"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("Resolved"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("Received"), A("Open")), S2(A("Draft"), A("Open")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition"), S2(S2(A("resolve"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("accept"), A("Open")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsFromStatus"), S2(S2(A("resolve"), A("Open")), S2(A("accept"), A("Received")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsToStatus"), S2(S2(A("resolve"), A("Resolved")), S2(A("accept"), A("Draft")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsTriggeredByEventType"), S2(S2(A("resolve"), A("AdminResolvesSupportRequest")), S2(A("accept"), A("AdminAcceptsSupportRequest")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S2(S3(A("CELL"), A("AdminResolvesSupportRequest"), PHI()), S3(A("CELL"), A("AdminAcceptsSupportRequest"), PHI())))))),
DEF("case:actions-of-an-entity-at-a-nested-status", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("actions"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("t1")), A("fixture:machines"))), PHI())),
DEF("case:actions-of-a-subtype-instance", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("actions"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("sr1")), A("fixture:subtype-machine"))), PHI())),
DEF("case:actions-of-an-id-no-machine-holds", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("actions"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("zz")), A("fixture:machines"))), PHI())),
"THE ROOT IS THE WORK (2026-09-21, task #122 item 4). csdp.md:14 states it: the legal transitions out of the current status are the ONLY HATEOAS affordances, and building an app is navigation of this machine. The served root answered the noun index instead -- 95 entity-type labels on support.auto.dev, a table of contents for storage -- and afforded nothing. This fixture declares two machines, one of them nested, and three instances: sr1 has fired nothing and stands at the Received that the seed descends to, sr2 has fired accept and stands at Draft, es1 stands at Raised. root:rows is the whole root as one value, a row per Object Type and Status carrying the instances standing there and the Event Types legally available to them, and those affordances are system:view_menu-s -- the same projection the actions verb answers for one entity -- so sr1 is offered the nested machine-s accept AND the outer machine-s inherited resolve, while sr2, already past accept, is offered resolve alone. root:work is that same value as the screen-s menus. The third case is the guard every other fixture and the base carrier rely on: a store that declares no State Machine Definition has an empty root:work, so its root is unmoved.",
DEF("fixture:work-root",
    K(S(S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusHasSubMachineStateMachineDefinition"), S1(S2(A("Open"), A("Open")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("ObjectTypeInstanceIsInstanceOfObjectType"), S3(S2(A("sr1"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("sr2"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("es1"), A("Escalation")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("StateMachineDefinitionIsForObjectType"), S2(S2(A("Support Request"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("Escalation"), A("Escalation")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusIsInitialInStateMachineDefinition"), S3(S2(A("Open"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("Received"), A("Open")), S2(A("Raised"), A("Escalation")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("StatusIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition"), S6(S2(A("Open"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("Resolved"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("Received"), A("Open")), S2(A("Draft"), A("Open")), S2(A("Raised"), A("Escalation")), S2(A("Closed"), A("Escalation")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsDefinedInStateMachineDefinition"), S3(S2(A("resolve"), A("Support Request")), S2(A("accept"), A("Open")), S2(A("close"), A("Escalation")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsFromStatus"), S3(S2(A("resolve"), A("Open")), S2(A("accept"), A("Received")), S2(A("close"), A("Raised")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsToStatus"), S3(S2(A("resolve"), A("Resolved")), S2(A("accept"), A("Draft")), S2(A("close"), A("Closed")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("TransitionIsTriggeredByEventType"), S3(S2(A("resolve"), A("AdminResolvesSupportRequest")), S2(A("accept"), A("AdminAcceptsSupportRequest")), S2(A("close"), A("AgentClosesEscalation")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("FILE"), S3(S3(A("CELL"), A("AdminResolvesSupportRequest"), PHI()), S3(A("CELL"), A("AdminAcceptsSupportRequest"), S1(S2(A("a1"), A("sr2")))), S3(A("CELL"), A("AgentClosesEscalation"), PHI())))))),
DEF("case:the-root-is-the-work-by-object-type-and-status", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("root:rows"), A("fixture:work-root")), PHI())),
DEF("case:the-root-offers-each-instance-its-legal-transitions", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("root:work"), A("fixture:work-root")), PHI())),
