"ONE NAME FOR A FACT TYPE, BY NORMA'S DCIL RULE (Sam, 2026-09-09). cn:dcil raises the first letter of every word of a name and touches nothing else: a word keeps its apostrophe (the possessive is not a new word), an abbreviation keeps its period, a hyphen or a space ends a word, and a word already cased stays. These are the three spellings on which lambda's relations and NORMA's disagreed on eu-law.",
