"A UNIQUENESS READS THE CELL A CLOSURE PUTS (2026-10-03, task #154). A head the closure derives keeps its rows in a top-level cell of its name, and its descriptor`s fifth slot stays empty until a commit is adopted, so cmd:viol_for over the descriptor saw no row. cmd:pop_desc hands it the cell`s rows where the store holds the cell, and the descriptor as it is where it holds none: here UcPair, unique per Function, whose cell holds two rows for f1, is a violation at role 1, and a descriptor holding those rows over a store with no such cell is the same violation.",
