"A UNIQUENESS OVER TWO ROLES OF THREE IS CHECKED (2026-10-03). MuTri is unique on its first two roles: rows a b c1 and a b c2 share the span, so the descriptor holds a violation that names it, (1, 2); rows a b c1 and a x c1 do not, though role 1 repeats in them and role 3 too. A uniqueness over all three roles holds whatever the rows are.",
