"A DEONTIC UNIQUENESS WARNS FOR THE KEY THAT REPEATS (2026-10-03). The store holds W, where a has two rows and b one, and W3, where a b has two rows and a x one. The obligation that each W have at most one value at role 1 warns once, for a; the one over roles 1 and 2 of W3 warns once, for a b. Neither asks whether an instance plays the role: that is a mandatory, which these are not.",
