"A LAP THROUGH A COMPOSITE COMES BACK, WHATEVER ORDER THE MACHINE IS WRITTEN IN (2026-09-25). Request`s machine starts at Open, a composite whose initial is Received; `accept` goes on to Draft inside Open, `resolve` is from Open to Resolved and `reopen` from Resolved back to Open. r1 was accepted, resolved and reopened, r2 resolved and reopened, and one lap brings both back to Received, the leaf Open is entered at. The fold used to fire transitions in the order the store listed them with every inherited copy last, so both read Resolved: the copies of `resolve` from Received and Draft fired after `reopen`. The second fixture declares the same machine in the reverse order and folds the same way, and main:fold_trs answers the one order for both: each status`s transitions after every status that can lead to it, the direct copy on the composite last.",
