"AN OBLIGATION OF AT MOST ONE IS NO UNIQUENESS OF THE FACT TYPE (2026-10-03). support`s `Support Thread is created from Support Request. *` has one uniqueness, `It is obligatory that each Support Thread is created from at most one Support Request`. Its descriptor carried that obligation as a uniqueness on the thread`s role, and the map, which reads alethic uniqueness only, laid out no table for it. So its rows were never stored, and after deploy B every thread failed its creator mandatory. The obligation stays in state:deontics, and the fact type takes the spanning uniqueness every population has. The answer is the descriptor`s uniquenesses, then the keys state:deontics holds.",
