"AND A SEMI-DERIVED HEAD`S DERIVED ROWS GO WITH THEIR SUPPORT (2026-10-02). NegS is marked semi-derived: it is asserted, and derived both from NegP joined to NegG and, for agent z, from each lapsed Layer. The walk goes on past the six writes to assert two NegS rows, derive one of them as well, and retract a derived row and an asserted one. Every head is compared with the closure of the facts asserted so far, written into the base and closed once (fixture:neg-ref), not with the closure of the walked store, which would start NegS from the derived rows that store holds.",
