"AND AS THE COMPILE HOLDS THEM, WHERE NO POPULATION IS FILED YET (2026-10-03). The in-place compile asks what it excludes of the readings` cells before it files them (compile:ip_excluded over the cells the reader wrote), and there a population is in its fact type`s descriptor alone: no FILE, and no cell of its own. fed:yielded_fts read the yields through system:pop_rows, which finds nothing there, so the compile held no cache to keep, left out the call counts the syncs wrote of a ** head a closure rule reads, and its closure wrote the head empty. The store below is that shape: the yields and the counts are in their descriptors only, and the count head, keyed on three of its four roles, is the Function`s cache all the same.",
