DEF("case:a-rest-leg-joins-on-every-subscripted-variable-it-shares", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("fixture:text-derived"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("TrigramIsTheReversalOfTrigram")), K(S2(A("i-ching.md"), A("Trigram(.Trigram Name) is an entity type.\nTrigram Name is a value type.\nPolarity is a value type.\n\nTrigram has bottom- Polarity.\nTrigram has middle- Polarity.\nTrigram has top- Polarity.\nTrigram is the reversal of Trigram. *\n\nEach Trigram has exactly one bottom- Polarity.\nEach Trigram has exactly one middle- Polarity.\nEach Trigram has exactly one top- Polarity.\n\n* Trigram1 is the reversal of Trigram2 iff Trigram1 has bottom- Polarity1 and Trigram1 has middle- Polarity2 and Trigram1 has top- Polarity3 and Trigram2 has bottom- Polarity3 and Trigram2 has middle- Polarity2 and Trigram2 has top- Polarity1.\n\nTrigram 'Force' has bottom- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Force' has middle- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Force' has top- Polarity 'Yang'.\nTrigram 'Field' has bottom- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Field' has middle- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Field' has top- Polarity 'Yin'.\nTrigram 'Shake' has bottom- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Shake' has middle- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Shake' has top- Polarity 'Yin'.\nTrigram 'Ground' has bottom- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Ground' has middle- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Ground' has top- Polarity 'Yang'.\nTrigram 'Gorge' has bottom- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Gorge' has middle- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Gorge' has top- Polarity 'Yin'.\nTrigram 'Radiance' has bottom- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Radiance' has middle- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Radiance' has top- Polarity 'Yang'.\nTrigram 'Bound' has bottom- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Bound' has middle- Polarity 'Yin'. Trigram 'Bound' has top- Polarity 'Yang'.\nTrigram 'Open' has bottom- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Open' has middle- Polarity 'Yang'. Trigram 'Open' has top- Polarity 'Yin'.\n"))))), PHI())),
"The smallest rule the general join reads that way: Box1 carries three legs, and `Lid1 fits Base1` shares Lid1 and Base1 with them. Box b2`s lid l2 fits s1 and b2`s base is s2, so b2 seals nothing; joined on Lid1 alone, b2 sealed l2.",
DEF("case:a-leg-that-shares-two-variables-is-joined-on-both", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("fixture:text-derived"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("BoxSealsLid")), K(S2(A("box.md"), A("Box(.Box Id) is an entity type.\nLid(.Lid Id) is an entity type.\nBase(.Base Id) is an entity type.\nTag(.Tag Id) is an entity type.\n\nBox has Lid.\nBox has Base.\nBox has Tag.\nLid fits Base.\nBox seals Lid. *\n\n* Box1 seals Lid1 iff Box1 has Lid1 and Box1 has Base1 and Box1 has Tag1 and Lid1 fits Base1.\n\nBox 'b1' has Lid 'l1'. Box 'b1' has Base 's1'. Box 'b1' has Tag 't1'.\nBox 'b2' has Lid 'l2'. Box 'b2' has Base 's2'. Box 'b2' has Tag 't2'.\nLid 'l1' fits Base 's1'. Lid 'l2' fits Base 's1'.\n"))))), PHI())),
"A star leg is joined the same way: `Box1 seals Lid1 iff Box1 has Lid1 and Box1 has Base1 and Box1 fits Lid1` folds its three legs on Box1, and two of them name Lid1. Joined on Box1 alone, b2 sealed the lid it has, though the lid it fits is l3.",
DEF("case:a-star-leg-joins-on-every-subscripted-variable-it-shares", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("fixture:text-derived"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("BoxSealsLid")), K(S2(A("box.md"), A("Box(.Box Id) is an entity type.\nLid(.Lid Id) is an entity type.\nBase(.Base Id) is an entity type.\n\nBox has Lid.\nBox has Base.\nBox fits Lid.\nBox seals Lid. *\n\n* Box1 seals Lid1 iff Box1 has Lid1 and Box1 has Base1 and Box1 fits Lid1.\n\nBox 'b1' has Lid 'l1'. Box 'b1' has Base 's1'. Box 'b1' fits Lid 'l1'.\nBox 'b2' has Lid 'l2'. Box 'b2' has Base 's2'. Box 'b2' fits Lid 'l3'.\n"))))), PHI())),
"AND A SUBSCRIPTED VARIABLE UNDER A ROLE NAME IS ONE VARIABLE (2026-10-03). `Hexagram1 is self-reversing iff Hexagram1 contains lower- Trigram1 and Hexagram1 contains upper- Trigram2 and Trigram1 is the reversal of Trigram2` names each trigram under its role name and then bare. The general chain read `lower- Trigram1` and `Trigram1` as two variables, never reached the reversal leg, and declined the rule as a body no form says, as it declined the proposal`s hexagram reversal and complement. Hexagram 1 is Force over Force and 27 is Bound over Shake, its reversal; 3 is Gorge over Shake, which is not.",
DEF("case:a-subscripted-variable-under-a-role-name-is-one-variable", S2(S3(A("COMP"), A("fixture:text-derived"), S3(A("CONS"), K(A("HexagramIsSelfReversing")), K(S2(A("i-ching.md"), A("Hexagram(.Hexagram Number) is an entity type.\nTrigram(.Trigram Name) is an entity type.\n\nHexagram contains lower- Trigram.\nHexagram contains upper- Trigram.\nTrigram is the reversal of Trigram.\nHexagram is self-reversing. *\n\n* Hexagram1 is self-reversing iff Hexagram1 contains lower- Trigram1 and Hexagram1 contains upper- Trigram2 and Trigram1 is the reversal of Trigram2.\n\nHexagram '1' contains lower- Trigram 'Force'. Hexagram '1' contains upper- Trigram 'Force'.\nHexagram '3' contains lower- Trigram 'Shake'. Hexagram '3' contains upper- Trigram 'Gorge'.\nHexagram '27' contains lower- Trigram 'Shake'. Hexagram '27' contains upper- Trigram 'Bound'.\nTrigram 'Force' is the reversal of Trigram 'Force'. Trigram 'Shake' is the reversal of Trigram 'Bound'. Trigram 'Bound' is the reversal of Trigram 'Shake'. Trigram 'Gorge' is the reversal of Trigram 'Gorge'.\n"))))), PHI())),
"AND A TYPE NAMED TWICE IN ONE LEG WITHOUT A SUBSCRIPT IS TWO VARIABLES (2026-10-03). support`s `Support Request is replied to if some Customer sends some Message and that Support Request has that Message and that Message responds to some Message` names Message twice in its last leg, the second a new message, and the reader drops `some` and `that`. A bare name is joined on the centre alone, as it was, so r1, whose message answers another, is replied to. Keyed on both, the message would have to answer itself, and no request would be. This case holds on main too: it keeps support`s rule as it is.",
