"FACTS ARE EVENTS (2026-10-02). A write records an Event for each fact it adds, asserted or derived, of a fact type the store classifies, at the write`s time, and closes again over the Events, so a rule that reads them answers in the same write. The fixture is a store cell by cell, written through main:assert0 and closed by store:closed_from as fixture:neg-write writes: EvX classifies (EventTypeIsClassified is its first role), EvM reads an Event`s type through EvX, as a classified Event moves a layer, and EvD is derived from EvR. fixture:ev-seen answers the layers EvM reached, the fact types the Events are of, and how many Events have a time. With no clock registered there is no time, and nothing is recorded.",
